WEBVTT

00:00.500 --> 00:07.562
Computer use agents look at screenshots and guess where to click. Browser agents read the page's accessibility tree instead.

00:07.912 --> 00:15.868
Osprey's UI machines give every native control a role and a label, so tests and agents can find the Play button by name, and press it.

00:17.068 --> 00:20.625
Every control in an Osprey UI machine carries a role and a label.

00:20.975 --> 00:29.088
The framework turns them into an accessibility tree: each live control with its role, its label, its bounds, and a slider's value.

00:30.288 --> 00:33.166
The test reads the labels on offer, then taps them.

00:33.516 --> 00:40.265
A tap is a real pointer press and release at the centre of the control's bounds, so a misplaced hit area fails the test.

00:40.615 --> 00:49.738
Tap at half way along the volume slider, and the volume becomes one half. Tap a quarter along the position, and the canvas letters read zero zero fifty.

00:50.938 --> 00:52.759
The kit is three small modules.

00:53.109 --> 01:03.782
Views reads the rendered view and the canvas lettering. Semantics reads the accessibility tree and works out pointer positions. Events builds the same event JSON a real host sends.

01:04.982 --> 01:11.180
The tests drive the application's real exported boundary, the same two functions the desktop host calls.

01:11.530 --> 01:18.180
The outside world sits behind effects, so a handler supplies a fake TV, and every run is deterministic.

01:18.530 --> 01:23.103
The same labels an AI agent would use to operate the app are the labels the tests use.

01:24.303 --> 01:27.639
An agent operating this app needs no vision and no coordinates.

01:27.989 --> 01:36.491
It reads the controls that are live right now, picks one by name, and acts. Templates.act sets a slider, or presses anything else.

01:36.841 --> 01:40.287
The labels it uses are the labels the tests prove on every build.

01:41.487 --> 01:48.533
Two things are not done yet. The tree is not mapped to the platform screen reader, so VoiceOver does not read the player today.

01:48.883 --> 01:55.864
And there is no ready-made server that exposes a running app's tree to an outside agent. Semantics and act are the pieces it would call.

01:57.064 --> 02:03.245
Osprey is actively evolving. Read the UI test kit's README, and run the casting tests yourself.
